-- Xenophon, Memorabilia: remove Dakyns's footnotes from the live chunks.
--
-- The Gutenberg text (eBook #1177, source_url on every row since
-- 20260930131125) sets each of Dakyns's notes as its own paragraph opening
-- " (n) " with one leading space, with the note's marker "(n)" in the text
-- above it. The corpus copy collapsed the line breaks, so each note ran
-- straight on from Xenophon's sentence into the next ("...corrupting the
-- young." (1) {oi grapsamenoi} = Meletus ... S. 5 foll. In the first
-- place, what evidence..."), and a retrieved chunk handed Dakyns's
-- cross-references and alternative renderings to a reader as Xenophon.
--
-- The notes were found in the source file, not guessed at in the flattened
-- text: 680 note paragraphs, counting nine indented paragraphs that continue
-- a note (Dakyns's alternative renderings after notes 36 and 37 of Book IV,
-- ch. 2, and Kuhner's two syllogisms after note 17 of ch. 6). Every indented
-- paragraph that follows a note was read before it was counted as one; none
-- is a verse quotation of Xenophon's. The markers "(n)" in the text go with
-- them. Dakyns's braces around transliterated Greek in his translation
-- ({episteme}, {GNOMI SEAUTON}) are his rendering of Xenophon's words and
-- stay.
--
-- Method. The source was whitespace-collapsed the way the chunks were, every
-- live chunk was located in it exactly (202 of 202), and the note and marker
-- characters inside each chunk were recorded as [offset, length] spans in
-- that chunk's own coordinates, which also handles a note cut in two by a
-- chunk boundary. Below, each changed chunk is checked against the md5 of its
-- current text, the spans are removed from the end backwards, runs of spaces
-- are collapsed, and the result is checked against the md5 computed outside
-- the database. Any mismatch raises and rolls the migration back.
--
-- Checked before applying: no marker "(n)" survives in any chunk; none of
-- the 680 notes survives; every cleaned chunk, whitespace aside, is a
-- stretch of the source with the notes removed; no two words are run
-- together.
--
-- Chunk boundaries, ids, section_label and locator are unchanged. 200 of the
-- 202 live chunks change; each original is kept as a deprecated row at the
-- end of the work before it changes. The changed chunks are re-embedded after this
-- migration.

-- For each chunk: check it, keep the original as a deprecated row at the end
-- of the work, then remove the notes. ci = chunk_index, b / a = md5 before /
-- after, s = [offset, length] spans, 0-based, in the chunk's own text.
do $$
declare
  rec record;
  sp record;
  t text;
begin
